  "title": "Santorini",
  "players": "2–3",
  "about": "Santorini — 2–3 players. Take turns; on your turn, move one of your two workers, then build with that same worker.\n\nMove: one space in any direction (diagonals too) onto an unoccupied space without a dome. A worker can climb at most one level up, and can step down any number of levels.\n\nBuild: on any unoccupied space next to the worker that moved — a level 1 block on bare ground, level 2 on level 1, level 3 on level 2, or a dome on level 3. A domed space is closed for good.\n\nWin by moving one of your workers up onto level 3. If you cannot move and build on your turn, you lose.\n\nSetup: the youngest player places both their workers first, then the others in turn. In this scene: pick your seat (Blue, Cream or Grey, by the workers' colours) with the Seat picker at the top right, then press a piece and drag it to carry it; it snaps to the board's spaces and stacks on whatever is already there. Hold Alt to put a piece down without snapping, Q / E to turn it.",
